// A path that holds a NUL byte is a runtime error for stat
// (spec/05-stdlib.md, Paths). A consumer that truncates the String returns
// nil, as for a path that does not exist, so a program cannot tell that it
// asked for another path.
// STATUS: error
// CHECK: before
// COVERS: path stat
print "before";
print stat("/tmp/loxpp_probe_nul_stat" + chr(0) + "tail");
